# Red that stays after the agent reconnects (Boss, 2026-10-30 00:42): a chat showed "needs attention", its agent
# reconnected and worked again, and the red stayed. Fictional Mac thread "Reconnect test", made by the production path
# stage by stage (--es reconnect dropped|back|done: macSettle, then a working status, then its answer; the row and dot by
# macThreadNow). Nothing reaches a Mac.
# 1. Dropped mid-request: needs attention, on the entry and in All chats.
fold folded
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es reconnect dropped
clearlog
log fixture reconnect dropped: [Failed]
expect Fictional long job
expect needs attention
shot reconnect-dropped-entry-cover
tap Show the tabs
expect Reconnect test
shot reconnect-dropped-tab-cover
# 2. The agent is back and working: the request runs again; no red anywhere.
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es reconnect back
clearlog
log fixture reconnect back: [Running]
expect Fictional long job
absent needs attention
tap Show the tabs
expect Reconnect test
absent needs attention
shot reconnect-back-tab-cover
swipefrom Reconnect test -0.70 0 500
swipefrom New chat -0.70 0 500
tap All chats
expect AT WORK
expect Reconnect test
absent needs attention
shot reconnect-back-all-chats-cover
key BACK
# 3. It answered: done, at rest, still no red.
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es reconnect done
clearlog
log fixture reconnect done: [Done]
expect Fictional job finished after the reconnect.
absent needs attention
shot reconnect-done-entry-cover
[phone] After the bundle: a Mac thread that drops mid-request (stop its runner briefly, or let the agent reconnect) goes red; once the agent works again its tab dot is green and its Agents page tile reads working, not "needs attention"; when it answers, both rest without red. A thread with a real waiting question or approval stays red/accent until he answers.
